        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Inspect the vehicle under natural daylight to reveal any surface imperfections, scratches, dents, or paint variations that artificial lighting might conceal.</span></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Compare every visible area with the high‑resolution pickup photographs taken at the origin. Use a side‑by‑side checklist that references each photo number and the corresponding vehicle part (e.g., front fairing, fuel tank, rear wheel).</span></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Document any new findings on a standardized condition report, noting the exact location, nature of the defect, and, if necessary, capture a supplemental photo for the record.</span></li>
